# [check-privacy] Production token hash list (PRIV-02, R6/D-08).
#
# Every entry below is the SHA-256 of a NORMALIZED real class A/B/C marker
# (lowercase + ё→е + Unicode NFC — see normalize() in check-privacy.mjs).
# This file intentionally stores hashes, never the plaintext values that
# produced them — the values were entered via
# "node scripts/check-privacy.mjs --add --hashes scripts/privacy-tokens.sha256"
# (or the equivalent scratch-only extraction script used to populate this
# list from pre-cleanup git history, per plan 37-04), which reads the value
# from a no-echo stdin prompt and never writes it to a file, commit message,
# or shell history.
#
# Recovery (R7 — fail-closed): the gate refuses to run if this file is
# missing or empty rather than silently skipping the check. If this file is
# ever lost, rebuild it via --add using the marker-shape checklists in
# .planning/phases/37-data-privacy/37-01-SUMMARY.md and 37-02-SUMMARY.md as
# the re-derivation source (never unaided recall).
#
# To add a new real value: run
#   node scripts/check-privacy.mjs --add --hashes scripts/privacy-tokens.sha256
# in an interactive terminal (never piped/CI), answer the class prompt
# (A/B/C), then type the real value at the no-echo prompt. The value is
# hashed and appended; it is never displayed or written anywhere in
# plaintext.
#
# Residual risk (D-08, accepted): SHA-256 of a short, low-entropy phrase is
# dictionary-attackable — this list is a stop-word list against accidental
# re-introduction, not cryptographic protection. The same values already
# exist unredacted in this repository's git history (PRIV-03, restoring a
# clean history, is deferred) — this file does not increase that exposure,
# it only prevents the same values from re-entering HEAD going forward.
#
# Format: one `<sha256-hex> <class A|B|C>` per line, sorted by hash.
